 ## Background
-This method is an extension of k-means clustering to partially defined data, based on the property that k-means can handle missing values by ignoring them during distance and mean calculations [LFWV03, cited in S1, unofficial]. It was applied to volume rendering compression in "Compressed Random-Access Trees for Spatially Coherent Data" [S1, unofficial].
+This method extends k-means clustering to partially defined data, leveraging the property that k-means preserves convergence when ignoring undefined components during distance and mean calculations [S1, unofficial]. It is used within brood-based vector quantization to compress residual blocks that extend beyond defined domain bounds [S1, unofficial].
 
